## plan
- set up a new django project and application.
- create the `entry` model in `models.py` with fields for title, content, last modified by, and last modified at.
- create the `edit` model to track changes made to entries.
- implement views in `views.py` to handle the following endpoints:
  - `get /entries`: retrieve a list of all entries.
  - `post /entries`: create a new entry.
  - `get /entries/{entryid}`: retrieve a specific entry.
  - `put /entries/{entryid}`: update an existing entry.
  - `get /entries/{entryid}/edits`: retrieve the edit history of a specific entry.
- set up url routing in `urls.py` to connect the views to the specified endpoints.
- configure the sqlite database in `settings.py`.
- ensure the application runs on port 0.0.0.0:5000 by modifying the runserver command.
